        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3046e578-428d-55a1-b5c2-c441932c36e5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: William T. Anderson, Jesse James, Bob Ford, Mary \"Mother\" Jones, William Quantrill\n- Events: Centralia Massacre, American Civil War\n- Places: Centralia, Missouri, Huerfano County Courthouse and Jail\n- Roles: pro-Confederate guerrilla leader, labor leader\n\nFacts:\n- The Centralia Massacre occurred at Centralia, Missouri on September 27, 1864 during the American Civil War.\n- The Centralia Massacre involved the capture and execution of twenty-four unarmed Union soldiers by pro-Confederate guerrilla leader William T. Anderson.\n- William T. Anderson, also known as \"Bloody Bill\" Anderson, lived from 1840 to October 26, 1864 and was one of the deadliest and most brutal pro-Confederate guerrilla leaders in the American Civil War.\n- Jesse James was a follower of William Quantrill and \"Bloody Bill\" Anderson.\n- Jesse James and associated followers were accused of participating in atrocities against Union soldiers and civilian abolitionists, including the Centralia Massacre in 1864.\n- The jail at the Huerfano County Courthouse and Jail held Bob Ford, who killed Jesse James, and labor leader Mary \"Mother\" Jones.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
